+   Concrete failure scenario: `_apply_mcp_secrets_ignore` still equates textual presence with effective exclusion. An adopter `.gitignore` containing `state/mcp_client_secrets/` followed by `!state/mcp_client_secrets/` is reported as already protected, while Git permits secret files to be committed. Unlike the posture entries, this security-sensitive path never calls `_gitignore_reassert_effective`; the unit test covers only symlink refusal. This affects fresh/recorded maintainer installs and pre-state maintainers opting into root delivery.  
